speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I would refer to clause 10, paragraph (b) which says:
-pay to producers of an agricultural commodity, directly or through such agent as the board may determine, the amount by which the prescribed price exceeds a price determined by the board to be the average price at which the commodity is sold in such markets and during such periods as the board considers appropriate;
I believe that in this clause we have the principle of deficiency payments. If the minister denies that there is a form of deficiency payments in that bill, perhaps he should explain what that clause does mean.
